  "implementation": {
    "mask": "Fixed block size8, retain up to2048 blocks. Input F16 index scores already carry causal negative infinity. Produce I8[rows,keys/8+1] drop mask, 1=dropped and0=retained. Finite scores and infinities admitted; NaNs outside this operation input contract.",
    "maxima": "Include keys/8+1 blocks, with an empty extra tail when keys divisible by8. Missing tail values negative infinity. Equal maxima retain the later FP16 payload, including signed-zero sign. Pin max((pos0+row+1)/rate-1,0)/8 to positive infinity. No maximum clamp changes the source pin.",
    "selection": "Reuse qualified radix FP16 index top-k with request-owned scratch. Mask membership matches pinned Torch.topk; unreachable negative-infinity blocks remain dropped after newest-block pinning. Selected-block scratch follows existing ordered-index top-k semantics.",
    "kernels": "Fuse maxima, pin and drop initialization; then existing top-k (one or two kernels); scatter selected reachable blocks. Three kernels without split or four with split. Private CUDA mechanics only.",
    "preflight": "Checked scalar workspace plan with unchanged output on failure. Exact view counts/types, canonical empty unused scratch, request identity, alignment, and pairwise overlap checked before writing any output. Caller supplies all buffers and budgets. No allocation, host transfer or completion fence inside operation.",
    "ownership": "Immutable architecture/model configuration unchanged. Mutable scores, mask and workspace remain request/session-owned. No global mutable workspace or GPU handles on model weights.",
    "limits": "Rows1..65535, logical keys16385..1048576, input stride>=keys, block stride>=keys/8+1, rate1..256, checked position end and newest-block range. Candidate source is only active beyond2048*8 entries."
  },
